#: ../../source/api/PyFlow.transfer_web.web_backend.server_backend.rst:2
#: 4e16e69f9ae9491a95bfcab9c70cfe24
msgid "PyFlow.transfer\\_web.web\\_backend.server\\_backend module"
msgstr ""

#: 15eb6d4006b3429a8fa230a2b460b1c5
#: PyFlow.transfer_web.web_backend.server_backend:1 of
msgid "Flask backend wrapping the PyFlow TCP server for the web tool."
msgstr ""

#: 3c413c9e37f94c7485dba6d4f96b9bf2
#: PyFlow.transfer_web.web_backend.server_backend:3 of
msgid "Two modes, one process:"
msgstr ""

#: 557b793ac8e441db86cf59cad5e85371
#: PyFlow.transfer_web.web_backend.server_backend:5 of
msgid ""
"``config`` mode: serves the server startup-configuration UI.  The UI "
"shows every ``TCP_Server_Base`` parameter with its default value; on "
"submit the config is written to ``.Flow_Web/setup_server.json`` (same "
"shape as ``flow_setup``'s ``setup.json``) and the TCP server class is "
"started."
msgstr ""

#: PyFlow.transfer_web.web_backend.server_backend:10
#: cb922669795b42c6ad5587b527c4356a of
msgid ""
"``status`` mode: serves the minimal status page plus the same "
"sidebar/input UI as the client frontend (forwarding disabled; native "
"sends to connected clients allowed).  Also exposes the HTTP API that "
"clients use to discover the TCP server address/port."
msgstr ""

#: 0c6784517a194d65926c71b7ce7f4836
#: PyFlow.transfer_web.web_backend.server_backend:15 of
msgid ""
"The backend monitors ``server.clients``: whenever a client connects or "
"disconnects it broadcasts the current instance list to every connected "
"client (``/web_clients_update``), and it re-checks the list every minute."
msgstr ""

#: 535e49236690482ebf574e6c65b10f39
#: PyFlow.transfer_web.web_backend.server_backend:20 of
msgid ""
"Inbound events (plain-text messages and file uploads arriving from "
"clients) are captured on the TCP server's receive threads through "
"``TCP_Server_Base``'s ``add_message_listener``/``add_file_listener`` "
"APIs, queued here, and polled by the frontend via ``/api/events``.  The "
"message listener reports every inbound line, protocol commands included; "
"the commands are dropped here, so the queue carries user messages only. A"
" file event carries the token of the saved file as well, so the chat can "
"link the name to ``/api/open_location``: the route hands the path "
"recorded for that token to the file manager of this host."
msgstr ""

#: 6ee75a9919554a3cb05d55c0f9dba653
#: PyFlow.transfer_web.web_backend.server_backend:30 of
msgid ""
"Authentication: anonymous visitors get a white landing page (the server "
"addresses and a login button; while a verification mailbox is configured,"
" also a registration button and a password-reset button); the "
"configuration and status pages need a session.  Accounts live in the "
"SQLite store ``.Flow_Web/flow_web.db`` (see `user_database`); the first "
"run seeds the ``admin``/``admin`` administrator and the frontend warns on"
" every login until those default credentials are changed.  Registration, "
"password reset and code-based client logins are delivered by the mailbox "
"configured from the startup-configuration page (see `mail_service`)."
msgstr ""

#: 14b91efc5192438eb9eb025aa4a50ef2
#: PyFlow.transfer_web.web_backend.server_backend:40 of
msgid ""
"Client accounts: the verification mailbox is the switch of the whole "
"client side.  While ``.Flow_Web/email_config.json`` holds a validated "
"mailbox the server is meant for public networks: the client web frontend "
"logs in through ``/api/client_login`` with a username/email, the account "
"password *and* a mailed verification code — both factors are required — "
"and receives a session token.  Re-entering the client web UI replays the "
"saved credentials and token through ``/api/client_verify``, which only "
"accepts them while they still open that account.  The token binds the TCP"
" connection the client opens (``/web_bind``) to that account, and the "
"instance list pushed to a client is limited to its contacts, so accounts "
"that never exchanged a contact request cannot see each other.  Without a "
"mailbox the server is an internal tool: clients connect without "
"registration or login, every client sees every other connected instance, "
"and the client account routes are closed — only the console administrator"
" keeps an account."
msgstr ""

